  "description": "meme-id: breaking_news_meme; hasOverallIntent: Harmful; overall-intent-description: The meme uses a photo of Anderson Cooper, a well-known news anchor, with the text 'breaking news' and 'the people don't believe our bullshit anymore.' The intent is to satirize or critique the perceived loss of public trust in mainstream media narratives. While not targeting any specific protected group, it is harmful because it undermines the credibility of professional journalism and may contribute to a broader erosion of trust in institutions, potentially leading to misinformation or apathy. The tone is cynical and dismissive, which can be damaging to public discourse and the integrity of news reporting.",
